{
  "code": "MATH-BS",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "The audit checks the Math Course Requirement (eight courses at the 100 level or above, MATH 56, PHIL 151 or 152 and one of STATS 116, 118 or 200 among them, plus 25 more Math units, with at most 10 units of single-variable calculus and 15 of the multivariable sequences), all letter graded, and four electives from Math courses numbered 101 and above or the approved outside list: three letter graded, and a fourth that may be an outside course taken for any grade (PHYSICS 41 or 61, offered only S/NC, can only be that fourth). The Computer Science Theory/Discrete Mathematics subplan is optional; if you pick it, its courses must be letter graded and also count toward the major's requirements. Honors is optional and adds requirement III and the MATH 197 thesis. Checked by hand: that six of the eight 100-level Math courses were taken at Stanford, an approved MATH 199 for honors III, and that STATS 118 and 200 are not used one in each requirement.",
  "nodes": {
    "arWTYxpX": {
      "why": "\"8 Math courses at the 100-level and above (including Math 56) plus 25 more units of Math classes (usually fulfilled using single and multivariable calculus).\" Notes: \"STATS 116 (No longer offered), STATS118 or STATS200 (at most one among STATS 118 and STATS 200, but not both, and neither if STATS 116 is being used) ... count as 100-level Math courses\" and \"The following course do not count toward the Math Course Requirement: course, course, MATH193X, MATH197, MATH198, and MATH199 (MATH 190, MATH193X and MATH199 can count towards the Elective Course Requirement\" (the electives text repeats that MATH190, MATH193X and MATH199 \"may only be counted toward electives\"). The two course names the Bulletin dropped, the two other courses that count as 100-level, \"Up to 10 units of Single Variable Calculus\" and \"at most 15 of such units\" from the multivariable sequences name no course codes, so they are checked by hand. The old 49-unit floor is not in the text and is dropped. Grading: \"All Math courses must be taken for a Letter grade.\" The page's course links, filled in, read: \"[PHIL 151], & [PHIL 152] count as 100-level Math courses\" and \"[MATH 190], [MATH 193], MATH193X, MATH197, MATH198, and MATH199\" do not count, so PHIL 151 and 152 join the eight and MATH 193 is excluded. \"Up to 10 units of Single Variable Calculus can be used as part of the Math Course Requirement\" and \"at most 15 of such units [the Math 50/60CM/60DM series] can be used towards the major\" are caps on the 25 units.",
      "replace": {
